    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nFor example, given this HTML:\n```html\n<div className=\"flex\" id=\"text\">text</div>\n```\nPressing `syat` to save the HTML surrounding.\n\nThen, on:\n\n`another text`\n\nPress `sa_y` to turn it into:\n\n```html\n<div className=\"flex\" id=\"text\">another text</div>\n```\nOr by pressing `sr` to change the current surround to the yanked surround, like `srty`.",
